  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Author of the Man Booker Prize shortlisted Swimming Home (2012), Debora Levy is an established playwright, novelist and poet. Diary of a Steak, Levy’s witty take on the hysteria surrounding ‘Mad Cow Disease’ is both highly amusing and deeply disturbing. Written in the form of the diary of a steak in a butcher’s shop, the narrative charts a progression into madness. Using typographical errors, omissions and forays into other languages, Deborah Levy describes a ‘mind that has been symbolically culled’. Referencing Freud, psychoanalysis, Jean-Martin Charcot, the English pride in madness and the herd mentality, Diary of a Steak is both thought-provoking and poignant."--Book Works website</subfield>
